 2. 💥 Scoop: First major Miller shakeup 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Stephen Miller in the presidential limousine after arriving in West Palm Beach on Friday night. Photo: Alex Wroblewski/AFP via Getty Images White House deputy chief of staff Richard Walters is leaving the administration, the first major departure in an expected staff shakeup as incoming chief of staff Stephen Miller takes charge, Axios' Alex Isenstadt reports. 

 Why it matters: The exit of one of outgoing chief of staff Susie Wiles' allies signals a changing of the guard inside the West Wing, with Miller's team poised to move into more powerful roles. Walters was one of Wiles' closest political lieutenants, with a relationship stretching back more than a decade. He's a veteran Republican operative who served as the longest-tenured chief of staff in RNC history.

 Walters resigned Friday, the same day that Trump announced Miller would replace Wiles. Read on . 

 
 
