 4. 📊 Data du jour: Massive turnout 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 Data : University of Florida Election Lab. Chart: Bruce Mehlman President Trump energizes Americans like no other national candidate in history:

 Bruce Mehlman points out in a special post-election edition of his popular " Six-Chart Sunday " on Substack that preliminary estimates of Tuesday's turnout was the second highest for a midterm in more than a century — topped only by 2018, during Trump's first term. "Love him or loathe him, Trump energizes midterm voters like nothing else — more than Vietnam, more than Watergate, more than civil rights," Mehlman told me.

 The largest share of eligible voters turned out in Maine (65.7%), Minnesota (65.2%) and Michigan (63.2%). All three states fueled the blue wave. 🔭 Zoom out: The past two presidential elections drew the most total votes (partly a function of population) of any in history. 

 2020: 158.4 million votes, when Joe Biden unseated Donald Trump. 2024: 155.2 million votes, when Trump defeated Kamala Harris. Explore the data ... Get Bruce Mehlman's Substack . 

 
 
