 5. 🇮🇱 Bibi rival tapped to form Israeli government 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Gadi Eisenkot, leader of the Yashar party, in Tel Aviv on election night, Oct. 28. Photo: Shir Torem/Reuters Israeli President Isaac Herzog announced yesterday that he'll task Gadi Eisenkot, leader of the Yashar party, with forming a new government, dealing a major setback to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.

 Eisenkot will have 28 days to form a new government. Why it matters: This is the closest Netanyahu has come to losing power since 2021. But deep divisions could still prevent rivals from forming a government, Axios' Barak Ravid writes. 

 Read on . 
 
