 8. 🐊 1 for the road: Holiday hot spots 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Kayak. Table: Sami Sparber/Axios Florida is home to five of this year's top 10 trending domestic holiday destinations, Axios' Sami Sparber writes from Kayak search data . 

 Why it matters: As airfares climb , travelers are "chasing sunshine without blowing the holiday budget," Kayak's Kayla DeLoache tells Axios. The big picture: Booking company Hopper reports travel this holiday season is on track to be the most expensive in at least a decade, largely because of soaring jet fuel costs.

 Domestic fares on Kayak averaged $417 for Thanksgiving and $418 for Christmas and New Year's — compared with last year's $317 and $351, respectively. Share this chart . 

 
 
